 # *Review Theseus changes*

-*Use the [Codex role adapter](../using-theseus/references/codex-tools.md#launch-a-role) with role `reviewer` and empty write scope. Use the selected development worktree as cwd.*
+*Review the supplied actual diff against the selected task and approved requirements. Inspect the committed base and head with read-only commands. Review specification alignment, regressions, test coverage, and potential data loss. Report any required updates to Implementation details for the orchestrator.*

-*Provide the scoped requirements, actual diff with base and head, prior findings and evidence of the required checks. Confirm that the changes satisfy requirements and preserve applicable behavior, including affected dependants. Report each finding with location, effect, evidence and whether it blocks acceptance. Report any mandatory verification still pending. Use outcome error while a blocker or mandatory verification remains unresolved.*
+*Use the [Codex role adapter](../using-theseus/references/codex-tools.md#launch-a-role) in read-only mode for the reviewer.*
+
+*Return JSON in the role result’s `response` with `base`, `head`, `diff_sha256`, `findings`, and `dispositions`. Copy the three Git-binding fields from the brief. Each new finding has `id`, `severity`, and `detail` identifying the requirement or risk, location, and evidence. Use `blocker` for unmet requirements, failed mandatory checks or confirmed substantial risks. Use `advisory` for other recommendations.*
+
+*For each prior blocker, return `id`, `status`, and `detail` with the verified basis. Use `open` for an unresolved finding, `fixed` for a confirmed correction on a changed diff, or `unsupported` after independently verifying a supplied challenge with Git evidence. Use empty arrays where applicable. A complete report uses outcome `success` even when it contains blockers. Preserve read-only access to the worktree, its index, and refs.*
