 # Code Review Reception
+
+## *Theseus review decisions*
+
+*Verify the findings against the affected code and requirements. For a disputed blocker, call `ReviewController.challenge` with the technical rationale and a verbatim citation (`side`, `path`, `line`, `quote`) in the reviewed base or head. The controller verifies the citation in Git and requires an independent reviewer to confirm the disposition.*
+
+*When `status(task_number)` asks for a fix, use its open blockers and `coder_override`. Two blocked rounds select `coder_heavy`. The caller prepares fixes for the same development worktree and owns publication. The controller leaves the candidate in place. Confirm the worktree still belongs to the task, the index and checkout are clean, and HEAD is the reviewed candidate before publishing a replacement. Execution accepts one replacement commit directly on the original dispatch parent with the same task subject/token and authorized files. Provide refreshed red/green evidence and run `run_execution` again to verify the replacement and re-review it. An extra fix commit on top of the previous candidate will fail the execution history check.*
+
+*After five unresolved rounds in an approach, analyze the failures before attempting another fix. Call `begin_approach` with the analysis and justified new approach. Submit a changed diff for review. All open blockers survive the transition and remain in Problems and the plan until a reviewer confirms their disposition. If the next approach needs a decision, retain the worktree and report the specific question.*

